{"table":"evidence","ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/evidence/ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","record":{"id":"ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","kind":"semantic_review","status":"not_run","command":[],"tool":"Ordinary source reconstruction; independent semantic acceptance not run","source_ids":["scalar-r2-26-source-order-parameter-regularity","scalar-r2-26-source-consequences","scalar-r2-26-source-qaoa-scalar","support_tex_regularity","circuit-r2-26-source-positive","eams2023_finite_step","bgmz2022_even_spin"],"subject_ids":["scalar.smooth_positive_density","scalar.fixed_strip_error_budget","circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","circuit.even_p_spin_obstruction"],"details":"Long §9.2 divides the positive-density bound using unit second moment and moment Cauchy–Schwarz. Long §7.1 bounds coupled Euler and martingale residuals by fixed-strip O(sqrt(delta)), retains shifted endpoint and terminal errors, and does not assert uniformity at one. Long §11.1 reconstructs a degree-uniform finite-horizon estimate from conditional variance recursion, node/cavity coupling and the exact edge decomposition, with spatial Lipschitz coefficients and actual common Gaussian initialization. Long §11.4 cites the independently inspected Basso–Gamarnik–Mei–Zhou fixed-depth theorem and proof. These are ordinary manuscript deductions or cited results; no graph status, Lean endpoint or Comparator acceptance is promoted."},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/evidence/ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:135459bb2961c95bd09cfce135666cd5a51fd11bb2c943829fdd7b81efdfef5d/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/2f85413164f06365ea0d825befee447650da71d54080d5dd65e78a708891c560","roles":["associated_record"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:cfbe950801fd334d8fd957243fa3b1f716ef609148c5f2ff97d44f9a6443d82c/paper